 "answer_text": "Found 2 gene records and 5 disease records for MLH1, MSH2 and colorectal cancer [6][7][8][9][10][11][12]. \n\nThis gene was identified as a locus frequently mutated in hereditary nonpolyposis colon cancer [1]. Functional assays using yeast and in vitro mismatch repair systems have been developed to analyze human MLH1 variants [2] [3]. MLH1 promoter hypermethylation can cause isolated loss of PMS2 expression in Lynch syndrome screening [4]. \n\nClinVar Variant Records\n\nMLH1 has also been studied in the context of laryngeal cancer oncogenesis [5]. \n\nGene records found\n\nGene NCBIGene:4292, name: mutL homolog 1 [6]. Gene NCBIGene:4436, name: mutS homolog 2 [10]. Gene symbol: MLH1 [13]. \n\nDisease records found\n\nDisease name: Muir-Torr\u00c3\u00a9 syndrome [7]. Disease name: Colorectal cancer, hereditary nonpolyposis, type 2 [8]. Disease name: Mismatch repair cancer syndrome 1 [9]. Disease name: Lynch syndrome 1 [11]. Disease name: Mismatch repair cancer syndrome 2 [12]. \n\nPubmed records found\n\nPubmed title: Impairment of MLH1 and CDKN2A in oncogenesis of laryngeal cancer [5]. Pubmed title: Functional analysis of human MLH1 variants using yeast and in vitro mismatch repair assays [2]. Pubmed title: Isolated Loss of PMS2 Immunohistochemical Expression is Frequently Caused by Heterogenous MLH1 Promoter Hypermethylation in Lynch Syndrome Screening for Endometrial Cancer Patients [4]. Pubmed title: Methylation Tolerance-Based Functional Assay to Assess Variants of Unknown Significance in the MLH1 and MSH2 Genes and Identify Patients With Lynch Syndrome [3]. Pubmed title: AI-generated MLH1 small binder improves prime editing efficiency [23]. \n\nClinvar records found\n\nClinvar title: NM_000249.4(MLH1):c.545+1271_677+737delinsCA [14]. Clinvar title: NM_000249.4(MLH1):c.453+625_545+920delinsT [17]. Clinvar title: NM_000249.4(MLH1):c.1418A>T (p.His473Leu) [19]. Clinvar title: NM_000249.4(MLH1):c.884+5T>A [21]. Clinvar title: NM_000249.4(MLH1):c.1039-1013G>A [24]. \n\nOmim records found\n\nDNA MISMATCH REPAIR PROTEIN MLH1 [15]. MLH1 [15]. \n\nClinical trial records found\n\nClinical trial name: The IMPACT Study - Identification of Men With a Genetic Predisposition to ProstAte Cancer [16]. Clinical trial name: Study of MK-3475 in Patients With Microsatellite Unstable (MSI) Tumors (Cohorts A, B and C) [18]. Clinical trial name: Surgery in Preventing Ovarian Cancer in Patients With Genetic Mutations [20]. Clinical trial name: Stand up to Cancer: MAGENTA (Making Genetic Testing Accessible) [22]. Clinical trial name: Durvalumab and Tremelimumab in Treating Patients With Microsatellite Stable Metastatic Colorectal Cancer to the Liver [25]. \n\nNote: this answer does not address the following entities named in the question: Colorectal cancer. Ask about them individually for a complete answer."
